WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Welcome back. Today we look at the light-dependent reactions of photosynthesis.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:17.000
These reactions happen in the thylakoid membranes inside the chloroplast.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:26.000
When a photon hits chlorophyll, an electron gets excited and moves along an electron transport chain.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Water is split in a process called photolysis, which releases oxygen as a by-product.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:50.000
The energy captured here is stored in ATP and NADPH for the Calvin cycle.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Next lecture we move on to the Calvin cycle and carbon fixation in the stroma.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Remember that the Calvin cycle needs ATP and NADPH from the light reactions to work.
